<p>Every house is different, so treat these as planning numbers, not a quote. Here's what moves each one.</p>

<h2>Seamless Gutter Installation</h2>

<p>Aluminum seamless gutters are the standard for North Alabama homes — fabricated on-site from continuous coil, so there are no leak-prone seams along the run. The total comes down to linear footage, the number of stories, how complex the roofline is, and whether any rotten fascia has to be fixed before the new gutters go up.</p>

<p>Size matters too. North Alabama gets 55+ inches of rain a year, and 6-inch gutters carry roughly 40% more water than 5-inch — which is why we usually recommend 6-inch gutters with 3x4" downspouts here.</p>

<p>For the full breakdown — materials, hanger spacing, and why three quotes on the same house can be thousands apart — see <a href="{{ '/articles/seamless-gutters-cost/' | url }}">what seamless gutters actually cost installed</a>.</p>

<h2>Gutter Cleaning</h2>

<p>Blue River Gutters charges $150-250 for most single-story homes and $200-350 for most two-story homes, with a $150 minimum. Height, roof pitch, pine needles, and how long it's been since the last cleaning all push the number up.</p>

<p>The cheapest quote usually skips the downspout flush, which is how debris ends up clogging underground drains. Our <a href="{{ '/articles/gutter-cleaning-cost/' | url }}">gutter cleaning cost guide</a> explains what a complete cleaning includes, and <a href="{{ '/articles/how-often-clean-gutters/' | url }}">how often to clean gutters</a> covers the right schedule for your trees.</p>

<h2>Fascia and Rotten Wood Repair</h2>

<p>Gutters are only as solid as the board they hang on. When fascia rots, hangers pull loose and gutters start to sag. Fascia repair typically runs $5-15 per linear foot, and most homes need 10-40 feet replaced — but the gutters usually have to come down and go back up, and rot that has reached the rafter tails is a bigger job.</p>

<p>See our <a href="{{ '/articles/fascia-repair-cost/' | url }}">fascia repair cost guide</a> for what drives the price and when gutters need to come down.</p>

<h2>Gutter Guards</h2>

<p>Gutter guard installation typically runs $7-15 per linear foot, or $1,050-3,000 for the 150-200 feet most homes need. Micro-mesh is the only type we've seen reliably stop pine needles. Under heavy tree cover, where cleaning is needed three or four times a year, guards can pay for themselves within a few years — faster under heavy pines. With light tree cover, they may not be worth it.</p>

<p>Compare the options in our <a href="{{ '/articles/best-gutter-guards/' | url }}">best gutter guards guide</a>, or see our <a href="{{ '/services/gutter-guards/' | url }}">gutter guard installation</a> service.</p>

<h2>Underground Drains</h2>

<p>On red clay, water that leaves the downspout often pools right back at the foundation. Underground drains carry it away, typically $10-25 per linear foot depending on soil conditions and digging, or $500-1,500 per downspout connection for a 20-40 foot run. Learn more about <a href="{{ '/services/underground-drains/' | url }}">underground drain installation</a>.</p>

<h2>How to Compare Quotes</h2>

<ul>
<li><strong>Compare the same job.</strong> Material gauge, gutter size, downspout size, hanger spacing, and old-gutter removal should all be on the quote.</li>
<li><strong>Watch the outliers.</strong> If one quote is 40% below the others, something is being left out.</li>
<li><strong>Check the terms.</strong> No deposit or a small one (10-20%) for special-order materials is standard. Requests for 50% or more upfront are a red flag.</li>
</ul>

